//
// A MISSING VALUE AFTER AN OPERATOR OR AN ASSIGNMENT IS REPORTED BY NAME.
// `x = ;` compiled and bound null, and `x += ;` compiled to a program whose later output
// vanished — no diagnostic either way, so the program answered wrong in silence.  `3 + ;`
// was refused, but as "missing argument for parameter 'v2' of `OpAddInt`", a name the
// author never wrote.  Each spelling now says what is missing and after which operator.
// Found while fixing loft#1800: the library parser refused `x = ;`, and loft itself did not.
// The controls — an open range (`v[2..]`), a trailing comma, `return ;` — still compile.
//
// @falsified-at: PENDING

fn main() {
  v = [1, 2, 3, 4];
  w = v[2..];
  u = [1, ];
  x = len(w) + len(u);
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: Expected a value after `=`
  x = ;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: Expected a value after `+=`
  x += ;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: Expected a value after `+`
  y = 3 + ;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: Expected a value after `*`
  z = (3 * );
  println("{x} {y} {z}");
}
